// Acme's book: the employment of `kinds.ax`, from the employer's side. Acme owns `payroll` and pays Alex out of it; Alex is a
// party here, as Acme is in the household's book (05-family), and the same kind says what follows.
//
// The employer's half of the payroll tax is in this book and not in the household's. Where the household's `alex-pay` is
// paid `into joint-checking`, this one is paid `from payroll`, and what the kind says of `employer` stands at `payroll`.

use std
use us
use us/ca

base USD

entity acme : employer
entity alex : person
  born   1988-02-10
